The release looks at every thread with units that waits without time and leaves each where it was.
A thread whose account reached a tick would wait on the spare or spent queue for good;
a thread with units that waits without time reaches a tick no earlier than the release.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place waits on another queue than its account says
Report: a place's account reaches a tick before the release
Witness: fuzz lend-lender-woken

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -838,7 +838,7 @@ static void release(uint32_t c)
         }
         /* One on the run queue that has lenders may have a request due sooner on its own account now. */
         if (p->queue == QUEUE_SPARE || p->queue == QUEUE_SPENT || (p->queue == QUEUE_RUN && place_thread(p)->lenders != 0)) {
-            place_settle(p);
+            (void)p;
         }
         /* A lender waits on no queue, and its account may give the borrowers it lends to, and on, time or a sooner request. */
         const struct thread *x = place_thread(p);
